WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.183
"How to Treat Body Odor with Diet"

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.700
Vision is not the only
sense associated with

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.340
physical attractiveness
and partner preference.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.600
Body odor signals a variety
of information on matters

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.968
such as eating habits,
hygiene, health, and more.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.720
Based on a survey of hundreds
of college students,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.820
men rated visual and smell
information as being equally important

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.260
for selecting a lover, while women
considered how their potential mates

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.680
smell to be the single
most important variable.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.580
In other words, women ranked
body odor as more important

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.136
for attraction than ‘‘looks.’’

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.200
I’ve talked about the concern

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.660
around aluminum-
containing antiperspirants.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.000
What can we do to make
ourselves smell better?

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.600
Clinical studies dating
back to the 1950s show

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.660
that chlorophyll can be used
to improve body odors.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.500
This led to a wave of commercial
chlorophyll deodorant products.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.800
But, as one chlorophyll
scientist lamented,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.440
“because of the unfounded,
fantastic, and sometimes

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.160
completely idiotic claims
made for chlorophyll

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.560
by the promotion
and advertising men,

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.940
the buying public as well as
the scientist will remain skeptical,”

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.453
and rightly so.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.760
To be an effective deodorant,
chlorophyll has to be taken

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.580
internally at doses
that far exceed those found

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.240
in so-called “deodorizing”
chewing gums and lozenges.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.900
Studies showing the elimination
of detectable underarm odors

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.941
used doses on the order
of 100mg a day.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.240
In other words, the amount
of chlorophyll one could get

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.840
in about a third of a bunch
of raw spinach.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.960
So, before slathering
aluminum onto your skin,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.440
I recommend first trying
to deodorize from the inside out

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.400
by eating a big salad every day,
which may improve your body odor

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.040
two ways, hitting
the chlorophyll threshold

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.357
and improving your health.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.060
There is a scent to disease.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.780
Some diseases result
in a characteristic odor

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.820
emanating from sick individuals.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.340
For example,
tuberculosis of the throat

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.320
makes you smell like stale beer.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.080
Typhoid makes you smell
like baked bread—

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.640
that doesn’t sound so bad—

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.517
though yellow fever makes
you smell like a butcher’s shop.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.280
But it’s not just infection.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.760
I mean evolutionarily,
wouldn’t it be advantageous

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.760
if you could smell
the first signs

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.460
of inflammation—immune
system activation—

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.560
to stay away from people before
they become contagious?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.700
What this team
of researchers did

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.640
was inject people
with endotoxin,

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.620
which is a highly
inflammatory component

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.600
of certain bacterial
cell walls.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.240
Caused a big spike
of internal inflammation,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.800
and the question is:

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.538
Could you smell it on people?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.420
Within just a few hours,
endotoxin-exposed individuals

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.760
had a more aversive body odor

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.542
relative to when they
were exposed to a placebo:

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:15.720
a significantly less pleasant
body odor within hours.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.040
Moreover, the more inflamed
they got, the worse they smelled,

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.560
providing the first
experimental evidence

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.447
that we can smell
inflammation on people.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.469
And guess where endotoxins
are found in the food supply?

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:34.440
Where bacteria
are found: in meat.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.413
And they’re not
destroyed by cooking.

00:03:36.413 --> 00:03:39.300
I have a whole series
of videos about that.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.940
We know meat
causes inflammation.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:47.074
So, does that mean
it makes people smelly?

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.340
You don’t know...until
you put it to the test.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.000
“The effect of meat consumption
on body odor attractiveness.”

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.320
Not just body odor,
but body odor attractiveness.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.300
For two weeks, male “odor
donors” were placed on a diet

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.200
that included meat or excluded
meat, a no-meat diet.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.860
And then, during the final
24 hours, they had pads taped

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.680
into their armpits
to collect their body odor.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.560
Then, the researchers
just needed some judges

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.911
to sniff the pads
from each of the men.

00:04:21.911 --> 00:04:27.519
So, fresh odor samples—hot off
the pits, less than an hour old—

00:04:27.519 --> 00:04:30.720
were assessed for their
pleasantness, attractiveness,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.760
masculinity, and intensity
by 30 women.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.940
A month later, the study
was repeated with the same guys,

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.305
but now following
the other diet.

00:04:41.305 --> 00:04:44.457
The same poor women
were used as judges.

00:04:44.457 --> 00:04:48.120
The men, incidentally,
were paid 2,000 in Czech currency

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.760
for their time
and “potential inconvenience

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.793
caused by the prescribed diet.”

00:04:52.793 --> 00:04:56.216
But the women who had to sniff
all those armpit pads?

00:04:56.216 --> 00:04:58.980
The raters were not paid
for their participation,

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.733
though did get a chocolate bar
after the second session.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:09.060
So, who had the most pleasant,
the most attractive body odor?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.400
The results showed
that “the odor of donors

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.460
when on the non-meat diet
was judged

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.140
as significantly more attractive,
more pleasant, and less intense.”

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.148
No difference was
noted for masculinity.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:27.300
The researchers concluded that meat
may have a “negative impact

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.000
on perceived body
odor hedonicity.”

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.520
In other words,
those eating more plant-based

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.734
evidently smell significantly
more pleasurable.

